#: ../../guide/syntax-reference.md:127
msgid ""
"`¬P(x) ∧ Q(x)` → `(¬P(x)) ∧ Q(x)` — negation binds tighter than conjunction"
msgstr ""
"`¬P(x) ∧ Q(x)` → `(¬P(x)) ∧ Q(x)` — Negation bindet stärker als Konjunktion"

#: ../../guide/syntax-reference.md:128
msgid ""
"`P(x) ∧ Q(x) → R(x)` → `(P(x) ∧ Q(x)) → R(x)` — conjunction binds tighter "
"than implication"
msgstr ""
"`P(x) ∧ Q(x) → R(x)` → `(P(x) ∧ Q(x)) → R(x)` — Konjunktion bindet stärker "
"als Implikation"

#: ../../guide/syntax-reference.md:129
msgid ""
"`P(x) → Q(x) ↔ R(x)` → `(P(x) → Q(x)) ↔ R(x)` — implication binds tighter "
"than biconditional"
msgstr ""
"`P(x) → Q(x) ↔ R(x)` → `(P(x) → Q(x)) ↔ R(x)` — Implikation bindet stärker "
"als Bikonditional"

#: ../../guide/syntax-reference.md:130
msgid ""
"`P(x) → Q(x) → R(x)` → `P(x) → (Q(x) → R(x))` — implication is right-"
"associative"
msgstr ""
"`P(x) → Q(x) → R(x)` → `P(x) → (Q(x) → R(x))` — Implikation ist "
"rechtsassoziativ"

#: ../../guide/syntax-reference.md:131
msgid ""
"`P(x) ∧ Q(x) ∧ R(x)` → `(P(x) ∧ Q(x)) ∧ R(x)` — conjunction is left-"
"associative"
msgstr ""
"`P(x) ∧ Q(x) ∧ R(x)` → `(P(x) ∧ Q(x)) ∧ R(x)` — Konjunktion ist "
"linksassoziativ"

